WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.397
- New in theaters this weekend,

00:00:01.397 --> 00:00:04.932
"Rambo: Last Blood," "Ad
Astra" and "Downton Abbey,"

00:00:04.932 --> 00:00:06.340
what will you see?

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.460
This is your "Weekend Ticket."

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:11.710
(mellow melodic music)

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.252
- I finally came home.
- Uncle John!

00:00:16.252 --> 00:00:19.473
- [John Voiceover] To defend
the only family I've ever know.

00:00:22.441 --> 00:00:25.069
- You must really want this girl.

00:00:25.069 --> 00:00:27.630
(dynamic upbeat music)

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.453
- All she's got is me.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:35.533
She's coming home.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.490
- John Rambo is back for
his fifth playful romp

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.027
in "Rambo: Last Blood."

00:00:41.027 --> 00:00:44.440
when John Rambo's niece is
abducted by the Mexican Cartel,

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:46.487
he decides it's time for revenge

00:00:46.487 --> 00:00:47.960
and if they're coming for him,

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:49.700
you'd better believe he's gonna set up

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:51.670
some "Home Alone" traps Rambo style

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:53.920
and bust out his trademark bow and arrow.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.530
If you're someone who's going in to see

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.960
how many kills Rambo
racks up in this movie,

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:59.592
here's the current kill stats by movie

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:02.080
with of course "Rambo IV" having the most,

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:05.240
leaving a lot of work for
Rambo this time around.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:06.710
This movie's for you if you're looking

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:09.262
for an intense revenge
action movie this weekend,

00:01:09.262 --> 00:01:11.890
if you love any of the
other "Rambo" movies

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:15.830
or if you're a fan of these
very real "Rambo" recap videos

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:17.873
Sylvester Stallone has been posting.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:20.963
- It's over!

00:01:20.963 --> 00:01:22.652
- Nothing is over!

00:01:22.652 --> 00:01:25.737
(melodic cinematic music)

00:01:25.737 --> 00:01:28.480
- [Sylvester Voiceover] Deep
in the jungles of Burma,

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:30.057
a happy group of mission--

00:01:35.137 --> 00:01:38.137
- [Eve] What are you thinking about?

00:01:39.061 --> 00:01:42.527
- [Roy Voiceover] I do what
I do because of my Dad.

00:01:42.527 --> 00:01:44.640
(melodic haunting music)

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.310
He was a hero,

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:48.793
he gave his life for the
pursuit of knowledge.

00:01:51.524 --> 00:01:53.463
Control, are you getting that, over?

00:01:54.926 --> 00:01:57.426
(low pulsing)

00:01:59.482 --> 00:02:03.149
(melodic suspenseful music)

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:12.772
(machine beeping quietly)

00:02:12.772 --> 00:02:14.980
- [Eve] It's crazy out there,

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:17.591
there's fires everywhere
and plane crashes,

00:02:17.591 --> 00:02:19.457
they're calling it the Surge.

00:02:19.457 --> 00:02:21.660
- "Ad Astra" comes out this weekend,

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:24.650
astronaut, Major Roy
McBride, played by Brad Pitt

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:27.000
survives an incident on the Space Station

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.410
only to learn that the incident

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:29.860
may be connected to his father,

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:33.070
whose spaceship and crew
went missing 30 years ago.

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:33.903
With this knowledge

00:02:33.903 --> 00:02:36.020
and the knowledge his
father is still alive,

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:38.110
he's sent on a mission to find his father

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:40.391
and find out what happened
and what he's been up to.

00:02:40.391 --> 00:02:42.390
I'll be honest, that's oversimplified,

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:45.230
because the movie is said
to be both introspective

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:46.860
and a visual spectacle.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:49.464
This movie's for you if you
like movies like "Interstellar,"

00:02:49.464 --> 00:02:52.160
you like a movie with
a lot of stars in it,

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:55.853
or you like movies with
a lot of stars in it,

00:02:57.554 --> 00:02:59.183
'cause it's in space.

00:03:01.197 --> 00:03:02.123
- [Man] Woo!

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:08.064
(melodic orchestral music)

00:03:08.064 --> 00:03:08.897
- Blimey!

00:03:12.018 --> 00:03:14.740
- The King and Queen
are coming to Downton.

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:15.573
- What?

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:24.263
- I want every surface
to gleam and sparkle.

00:03:26.779 --> 00:03:29.712
- A Royal luncheon, a parade and a dinner,

00:03:29.712 --> 00:03:31.373
I'm going to have to sit down.

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:34.280
- Tell your driver to ready the car

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:37.610
to take you to see "Downton
Abbey" in theaters this weekend.

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:39.320
In a continuation of the "Downton Abbey"

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:41.050
television series from BBC,

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:43.620
the Crawley family and their
staff are readying the estate

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:45.080
for a visit from non other

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:47.770
than the King and Queen of England.

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:49.810
This important visit is
sure to send the Abbey

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:52.560
into just as much drama
as we've come to expect

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.730
from the six seasons of the show.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:57.790
This movie's for you if you
love a good period piece,

00:03:57.790 --> 00:03:59.555
you're a fan of the
"Downton Abbey" TV show

00:03:59.555 --> 00:04:01.870
and you wanna see what happens next

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:03.930
or you figure since it's 2019,

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:06.312
they gotta sneak a Yaaas
Queen joke in there somewhere

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:08.300
and you've just gotta see that.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.568
That is your "Weekend Ticket!"

00:04:09.568 --> 00:04:10.401
What will you see?

00:04:10.401 --> 00:04:11.930
And check back next week

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:15.090
